WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.553
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
2: Celebrations and Festivals.

2
00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:10.364
In this unit you will explore celebrations
and festivals from around the world,

3
00:00:10.444 --> 00:00:17.130
with a special focus on traditions that matter
to communities across East Africa and beyond.

4
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.483
Festivals bring people together.

5
00:00:19.563 --> 00:00:25.955
They remind us of our history, our values,
and the things that make each culture unique.

6
00:00:26.035 --> 00:00:33.457
Whether it is the joy of a national independence
day, the colourful lanterns of a harvest celebration,

7
00:00:33.537 --> 00:00:39.047
or the excitement of a local sports
day, every festival has a story to tell.

8
00:00:39.127 --> 00:00:45.225
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:45.305 --> 00:00:53.475
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand texts about different festivals and celebrations.

10
00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:59.555
You will also use prepositions of time (in,
on, at) correctly in speech and writing.

11
00:00:59.635 --> 00:01:05.635
You will also recognise and form compound
adjectives (hand-made, brightly-coloured).

12
00:01:05.715 --> 00:01:08.313
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:15.605
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: benevolent,
charismatic, determined, diligent, enthusiastic, industrious.

14
00:01:15.685 --> 00:01:20.570
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:24.431
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:24.511 --> 00:01:32.087
The reading sequence includes Festivals That Bring Us
Together, part 1 and Festivals That Bring Us Together, part 2.

17
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.011
Read actively.

18
00:01:33.091 --> 00:01:37.565
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:37.645 --> 00:01:41.855
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:46.435
The first language focus is
Prepositions of Time: In, On and At.

21
00:01:46.515 --> 00:01:53.734
Prepositions of time tell your reader exactly when
something happens: in holds long stretches of time,

22
00:01:53.814 --> 00:01:58.886
on lands on particular days and dates,
and at points to precise moments.

23
00:01:58.966 --> 00:02:06.686
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:06.766 --> 00:02:11.125
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Compare Two Festivals.

25
00:02:11.205 --> 00:02:15.701
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:15.781 --> 00:02:19.184
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:22.804
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:22.884 --> 00:02:24.515
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:24.595 --> 00:02:31.882
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:31.962 --> 00:02:35.454
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:43.714
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
